PART B - CLASS IDENTIFICATION

ACCEPTED CLASSES

1. Product
   Stores common product information.

2. Book
   Represents books sold by the bookshop.

3. Magazine
   Represents magazines sold by the bookshop.

4. CD
   Represents CDs sold by the bookshop.

5. Customer
   Stores customer information.

6. PersonalCustomer
   Represents personal customers.

7. BusinessCustomer
   Represents business customers.

8. Order
   Stores customer orders.

9. Shipment
   Manages shipments of ordered products.

10. Payment
    Records customer payments.

11. Invoice
    Represents invoices for business customers.

12. CreditCard
    Represents credit card payment details.

13. Report
    Represents product reports.


REJECTED NOUNS AND REASONS

1. Online Bookshop
   Represents the overall system boundary.

2. Price
   Attribute of Product.

3. Title
   Attribute of Product.

4. Author
   Attribute of Book.

5. Number of Pages
   Attribute of Book or Magazine.

6. Artist
   Attribute of CD.

7. Type
   Attribute describing a product.

8. Registered Customer
   Registration status of Customer.

9. Delivery
   Process handled through Order and Shipment.

10. Contact Information
    Attributes of Customer.

11. Personal Information
    Attributes of Customer.

12. Authentication
    System behavior rather than a core entity.


NOTE ON THE FIVE RULES

